      "refersTo": "",
      "description": "One-line underline tabs; the active one has a 2px blue underline.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-tabs\" role=\"tablist\"><button class=\"ds-tab is-active\" role=\"tab\">Content</button><button class=\"ds-tab\" role=\"tab\">Attributes</button><button class=\"ds-tab\" role=\"tab\">Evidence</button><button class=\"ds-tab\" role=\"tab\">Validations (21)</button><button class=\"ds-tab\" role=\"tab\">Review</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-tabs{font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;display:flex;gap:20px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border,#d1d9e1);overflow-x:auto;scrollbar-width:none}.ds-tab{flex:none;margin-bottom:-1px;padding:8px 2px;border:0;border-bottom:2px solid transparent;background:transparent;color:var(--muted-foreground,#5f7281);font-size:14px;font-weight:500;cursor:pointer}.ds-tab:hover{color:var(--foreground,#11171c)}.ds-tab.is-active{border-bottom-color:var(--primary,#2272b4);color:var(--foreground,#11171c);font-weight:600}.ds-tab:focus-visible{outline:none;box-shadow:0 0 0 2px var(--ring,#2272b4)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Status Tags",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "tag-warning",
      "description": "4px rectangular tone tags, always icon plus label.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-tags\"><span class=\"ds-tag ds-tag-warning\"><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3\"/><path d=\"M12 9v4\"/><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"/></svg>Needs review</span><span class=\"ds-tag ds-tag-success\"><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><path d=\"m9 12 2 2 4-4\"/></svg>Approved</span><span class=\"ds-tag ds-tag-danger\"><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><path d=\"m15 9-6 6\"/><path d=\"m9 9 6 6\"/></svg>Rejected</span><span class=\"ds-tag ds-tag-info\"><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><path d=\"m9 12 2 2 4-4\"/></svg>Enriched</span><span class=\"ds-tag ds-tag-outline\">GTIN 7896067227749</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-tags{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px}.ds-tag{font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;padding:2px 8px;border:1px solid transparent;border-radius:4px;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;white-space:nowrap}.ds-tag-warning{background:var(--warning-soft,#fff4d6);color:var(--warning,#8a5100)}.ds-tag-success{background:var(--success-soft,#e9f6ec);color:var(--success,#277c43)}.ds-tag-danger{background:var(--danger-soft,#fcebee);color:var(--destructive,#c82d4c)}.ds-tag-info{background:var(--info-soft,#f1effb);color:var(--info,#5b4fb8)}.ds-tag-outline{border-color:var(--border,#d1d9e1);color:var(--foreground,#11171c)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Summary Panel",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "panel",
      "description": "One bordered panel of figures split by 1px dividers.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-summary\"><div class=\"ds-fig\"><h2>Products</h2><p class=\"ds-val\">1,284</p><p class=\"ds-det\">in the catalog</p></div><div class=\"ds-fig\"><h2>Enriched</h2><p class=\"ds-val\">912</p><p class=\"ds-det\">with generated content</p></div><div class=\"ds-fig\"><h2>Needs review</h2><p class=\"ds-val\">57</p><p class=\"ds-det\">waiting for a curator</p></div><div class=\"ds-fig\"><h2>Average quality</h2><p class=\"ds-val\">—</p><p class=\"ds-det\">no product scored yet</p></div></section>",
      "css": ".ds-summary{font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1px;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid var(--border,#d1d9e1);border-radius:8px;background:var(--border,#d1d9e1)}.ds-fig{padding:20px;background:var(--card,#fff)}.ds-fig h2{margin:0;font-size:14px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-0.025em;color:var(--muted-foreground,#5f7281)}.ds-val{margin:8px 0 0;font-size:24px;line-height:32px;font-weight:600;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--foreground,#11171c)}.ds-det{margin:4px 0 0;font-size:12px;line-height:20px;color:var(--muted-foreground,#5f7281)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Data Table",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "table-header",
      "description": "Gray header row, name is the row link, numbers right-aligned.",
      "html": "<table class=\"ds-table\"><thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>Status</th><th class=\"num\">Quality</th><th class=\"num\">Coverage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"#\">Refrigerator Panasonic NR-BT41PD1XA</a></td><td><span class=\"ds-tag-w\">Needs review</span></td><td class=\"num\">34.8%</td><td class=\"num\">75%</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"#\">Washer Electrolux LES13</a></td><td><span class=\"ds-tag-n\">Pending</span></td><td class=\"num\">—</td><td class=\"num\">—</td></tr></tbody></table>",
      "css": ".ds-table{font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px;color:var(--foreground,#11171c);border:1px solid var(--border,#d1d9e1)}.ds-table thead{background:var(--muted,#f6f7f9)}.ds-table th{height:36px;padding:0 12px;text-align:left;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted-foreground,#5f7281)}.ds-table td{padding:10px 12px;border-top:1px solid var(--border,#d1d9e1)}.ds-table .num{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-table a{color:inherit;font-weight:500;text-decoration:none}.ds-table a:hover{color:var(--primary,#2272b4);text-decoration:underline}.ds-table a:focus-visible{outline:none;box-shadow:0 0 0 2px var(--ring,#2272b4)}.ds-tag-w,.ds-tag-n{display:inline-flex;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;font-size:12px;font-weight:500}.ds-tag-w{background:var(--warning-soft,#fff4d6);color:var(--warning,#8a5100)}.ds-tag-n{border:1px solid var(--border,#d1d9e1)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Native to the Workspace",
    "overview": "BrickFill is the Databricks workspace product UI, played straight. The curator opens the app from the workspace and\nfinds no seam: the left sidebar, the gray table headers, the 4px status tags, the underline tabs and the one blue\nbutton act like the rest of Databricks. Attention goes to the values and their proof. The next decision is always the\nblue button.\n\nThe system is Databricks AppKit UI (shadcn components on Tailwind v4), themed through its CSS variables in\n`app/brickfill/client/src/index.css`. An unlayered convention layer keyed on each component's `data-slot` applies the\nworkspace conventions to the AppKit components themselves:\n- borders instead of card shadows;\n- rectangular tags;\n- 32px controls;\n- gray table headers;\n- underline tabs.\n\nNew screens inherit all of this by using the AppKit components and do not restyle them locally. The world is cool and\nexact: white surfaces, a cool gray secondary surface, near-black slate text, 1px cool-gray borders, and workspace\ndensity. The one warm note is the brick fill of the BrickFill mark.\n\nIt replaces an earlier warm workbench world (cream paper, terracotta action color, soft pill badges, top navigation).\nNone of those devices carry over.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "White and cool gray surfaces, slate text, 1px cool borders; flat panels with no shadow at rest.",
      "Databricks action blue for the primary action, the current place, links, selection and focus, and nothing else.",
      "Status tags are 4px rectangles: a soft tone surface, same-hue text, an icon and a label.",
      "The system sans at workspace density: 14px controls and tables, 32px controls with a mouse, 44px on touch.",
      "A fixed 240px left sidebar on desktop; a top bar with a sheet on phones.",
      "Light and dark themes with their own values (dark is Databricks' navy-slate, not an inversion), and an optional customer accent that replaces only the blue."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Blue Rule",
        "body": "Blue means \"act here\", \"you are here\" or \"go there\": the primary action, the current tab and\nsidebar item, links, focus and selection. Nothing that only describes a state is blue. One filled blue button per\narea.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Never Color Alone Rule",
        "body": "Every status carries an icon and a label next to its tone:\n- CircleDashed for pending;\n- Sparkles for enriched;\n- TriangleAlert for review required;\n- Eye for in review;\n- CircleCheck for approved;\n- CircleX for rejected.\n\nA grayscale screenshot must still be readable.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Warm Note Rule",
        "body": "The mark's brick is the only warm brand color on the page. The sanctioned exceptions are\namber as the warning tone and in charts, and Firecrawl's own orange inside the \"How it works\" dialog as partner\ncredit.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Twin Dark Rule",
        "body": "The dark palette is written twice in `index.css`, once for a `.dark` class and once for\n`prefers-color-scheme: dark`. `theme.test.ts` fails if the two differ, so change both together.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Inherited Line Rule",
        "body": "Paragraphs inherit the line height of their context. AppKit's 1.75rem prose line height\nis reset in `@layer base` so table rows and lists stay single-height; reading text sets its own (1.75rem).",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Figures Rule",
        "body": "Percentages, counts, page numbers and step numbers use tabular numerals.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Border, Not Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Anything that sits in the page is separated by a border or a tone step, never a\nshadow. A shadow means \"this floats\".",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use the AppKit components and let the `data-slot` convention layer in `index.css` set their workspace look. Change the layer, not individual screens.",
      "Do keep Action Blue for the primary action, the current place, links, focus and selection, with one filled blue button per area.",
      "Do draw statuses as 4px tone tags with an icon and a label.",
      "Do put the page title, a one-line description and the page's actions (including the one RefreshButton) on the title row.",
      "Do right-align numeric columns, use tabular numerals, and show \"—\" for a value that was never measured.",
      "Do separate panels with a 1px Cool Border, give fields the 3:1 Field Outline, and keep shadows for floating layers.",
      "Do keep 32px controls for a mouse and 44px targets for touch, and turn action tables into labeled stacked blocks below 1024px.",
      "Do change `.dark` and the `prefers-color-scheme: dark` block together."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't draw a status in Action Blue, or add a status hue outside the four tones.",
      "Don't use pills for status or identifier tags; tags are 4px rectangles.",
      "Don't add shadows to panels, buttons or fields, nest cards, or add colored side or top stripes.",
      "Don't use segmented-track tabs or wrap the tab row.",
      "Don't introduce warm surfaces or a warm accent; the brick of the mark stays the only warm brand note.",
      "Don't add an arrow or \"open\" column to a table whose row is already a link.",
      "Don't add glows, gradients or gradient text to sell the AI. Show the evidence instead."
    ]
  }
}